IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`

-- Employment Insurance Regulations (SOR/96-332), regulations 2 to 9: Insurable Employment. Piece er1, layer 1.
-- Text: the unofficial plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws consolidation current to 2026-09-30
-- (../../registers/source-bundle/SOR-96-332.txt). Nothing here is verified against the official text. `src:N` is a line of that file.
-- Instrument: the Regulations. They are made under subsections 5(4), (6) and (7) of the Act (src:9), and the core
-- (eia-core-insurable-employment) takes their results as BOOLEAN inputs:
--   s 5(1)(d)                 `employment included by regulations made under subsection (4) or (5)`
--                             <- `reg 2 to 6 employment included in insurable employment` below
--   s 5(2)(c)                 `included by regulations made under paragraph 5(4)(d)`  <- `reg 2(1) ...` below
--   s 5(2)(d) and (e)         `included by regulations made under paragraph 5(4)(e)` and `(f)`  <- `reg 3(1) ...` below
--   s 5(2)(h)                 `employment excluded by regulations made under subsection (6)`
--                             <- `reg 7 to 9 employment excluded from insurable employment` below
-- Each paragraph of regs 4 to 8 is a rule of its own with the facts the person can state as plain inputs; a thing the
-- text asks of an office (the Commission "enters into an agreement") is a BOOLEAN input named for what happened.

§ `Regulation 2 - employment by a province`

-- src:51 | 2 (1) Employment in Canada by Her Majesty in right of a province that would, except for paragraph 5(2)(c) of the Act, be insurable employment is included in insurable employment if the government of the province enters into an agreement with the Commission whereby that government agrees to waive exclusion and to insure all its employees engaged in such employment.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 2(1) (src:51)
-- Plain gloss: work for a provincial government, which the Act excludes from insurable employment (s 5(2)(c)), counts
-- as insurable if the province has made an agreement with the Commission to give up that exclusion and to insure all
-- its employees in such work. "Would, except for paragraph 5(2)(c) of the Act, be insurable employment" is one input:
-- the core's `s 5(1)` and the other paragraphs of `s 5(2)` decide it. The meaning of "employment ... by Her Majesty in
-- right of a province" is narrowed by reg 2(2), which this rule calls. Reading of "enters into an agreement ...
-- whereby that government agrees to waive exclusion and to insure all its employees engaged in such employment": one
-- agreement with both undertakings (fork F2 in NOTES.md).
-- src:52 | (2) For greater certainty, employment in Canada by Her Majesty in right of a province, for the purposes of subsection (1), includes only employment in Canada of employees who are appointed and remunerated under an Act governing that province's public service, or who are employed in Canada by a corporation, commission or other body that is an agent of Her Majesty in right of the province.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 2(2) (src:52)
-- Plain gloss: for reg 2(1), provincial government work means only work in Canada by employees who are appointed and paid
-- under the province's public service Act, or who work for a body that is the province's agent.
GIVEN `the employment is in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employee is appointed under an Act governing that province's public service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employee is remunerated under an Act governing that province's public service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employee is employed in Canada by a corporation, commission or other body that is an agent of Her Majesty in right of the province` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 2(2) employment by Her Majesty in right of a province, for the purposes of subsection (1)` IF
        `the employment is in Canada`
    AND (   (   `the employee is appointed under an Act governing that province's public service`
            AND `the employee is remunerated under an Act governing that province's public service`)
         OR `the employee is employed in Canada by a corporation, commission or other body that is an agent of Her Majesty in right of the province`)

-- src:51 | 2 (1) Employment in Canada by Her Majesty in right of a province that would, except for paragraph 5(2)(c) of the Act, be insurable employment is included in insurable employment if the government of the province enters into an agreement with the Commission whereby that government agrees to waive exclusion and to insure all its employees engaged in such employment.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 2(1) (src:51)
GIVEN `the employment is in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employee is appointed under an Act governing that province's public service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employee is remunerated under an Act governing that province's public service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employee is employed in Canada by a corporation, commission or other body that is an agent of Her Majesty in right of the province` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employment would, except for paragraph 5(2)(c) of the Act, be insurable employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the government of the province enters into an agreement with the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `by which the government agrees to waive exclusion` IS A BOOLEAN
      `and to insure all its employees engaged in such employment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 2(1) employment in Canada by Her Majesty in right of a province` IF
        `reg 2(2) employment by Her Majesty in right of a province, for the purposes of subsection (1)`
            `the employment is in Canada`
            `the employee is appointed under an Act governing that province's public service`
            `the employee is remunerated under an Act governing that province's public service`
            `the employee is employed in Canada by a corporation, commission or other body that is an agent of Her Majesty in right of the province`
    AND `the employment would, except for paragraph 5(2)(c) of the Act, be insurable employment`
    AND `the government of the province enters into an agreement with the Commission`
    AND `by which the government agrees to waive exclusion`
    AND `and to insure all its employees engaged in such employment`

§ `Regulation 3 - employment by a foreign government or an international organization`

-- Reg 3(2) mentions "June 30, 1996" only to say which version of the old Unemployment Insurance Regulations a consent was
-- given under; it is a description of the consent, so it stays inside the wording of the BOOLEAN input below.
-- src:54 | (2) Where a consent has been given pursuant to the Unemployment Insurance Regulations, as they read immediately before June 30, 1996, and has not been revoked, it shall be considered to be a consent referred to in subsection (1).
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 3(2) (src:54)
-- Plain gloss: a consent that a foreign government or international organization gave under the old Unemployment
-- Insurance Regulations (as they stood immediately before June 30, 1996) and has not revoked still counts as the
-- consent that reg 3(1) asks for.
GIVEN `a consent has been given pursuant to the Unemployment Insurance Regulations, as they read immediately before June 30, 1996` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the consent has been revoked` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 3(2) the consent is considered to be a consent referred to in subsection (1)` IF
        `a consent has been given pursuant to the Unemployment Insurance Regulations, as they read immediately before June 30, 1996`
    AND NOT (`the consent has been revoked`)

-- src:53 | 3 (1) Employment in Canada by the government of a country other than Canada or of any political subdivision of that other country, or by an international organization, that would, except for paragraphs 5(2)(d) and (e) of the Act, be insurable employment, may be included in insurable employment if the employing government or the international organization, as the case may be, consents in writing to its inclusion.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 3(1) (src:53)
-- Plain gloss: work in Canada for a foreign government (or one of its political subdivisions) or for an international
-- organization, which the Act excludes (s 5(2)(d) and (e)), may be treated as insurable if the employer agrees in
-- writing. "May be included ... if the employing government or the international organization consents in writing":
-- read as including the employment when it consents (the consent is the only condition the text states; fork F3).
-- "International organization" is reg 1(2) (`reg 1(2) international organization`, this piece). The same result
-- feeds the core's `included by regulations made under paragraph 5(4)(e)` for a foreign government and
-- `... 5(4)(f)` for an international organization.
GIVEN `the employment is in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer is the government of a country other than Canada or of a political subdivision of that other country` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer is an international organization` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employment would, except for paragraphs 5(2)(d) and (e) of the Act, be insurable employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employing government or the international organization consents in writing to its inclusion` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the consent is considered to be a consent referred to in subsection (1) by reg 3(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 3(1) employment by a foreign government or an international organization` IF
        `the employment is in Canada`
    AND (   `the employer is the government of a country other than Canada or of a political subdivision of that other country`
         OR `the employer is an international organization`)
    AND `the employment would, except for paragraphs 5(2)(d) and (e) of the Act, be insurable employment`
    AND (   `the employing government or the international organization consents in writing to its inclusion`
         OR `the consent is considered to be a consent referred to in subsection (1) by reg 3(2)`)

§ `Regulation 4 - employment on a ship outside Canada`

-- src:55 | 4 Employment on a ship outside Canada or partly outside Canada that would be insurable employment if it were in Canada is included in insurable employment if that employment is
-- src:56 | (a) on a ship of Canadian registry or licence, except where that ship is regularly employed in voyages between ports outside Canada and has been chartered to a person resident outside Canada; or
-- src:57 | (b) on a ship, other than a ship of Canadian registry or licence, where
-- src:58 | (i) the ship has been chartered to a person resident in Canada and is regularly employed in voyages from a port in Canada,
-- src:59 | (ii) the operation of the ship is principally controlled in Canada and regularly employed in voyages from a port in Canada and the owner or managing owner of the ship resides or has a place of business in Canada, or
-- src:60 | (iii) any employment on that ship is subject to the provisions of the Act by virtue of an agreement between the Government of Canada and the government of the jurisdiction in which that ship is registered.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 4 (src:55-60)
-- Plain gloss: work on a ship outside Canada, or partly outside, that would be insurable if done in Canada counts as
-- insurable if (a) the ship is of Canadian registry or licence (unless it regularly sails between ports outside Canada
-- and is chartered to someone resident outside Canada), or (b) the ship is not of Canadian registry or licence but is
-- chartered to a resident of Canada and sails regularly from a Canadian port, or is run mainly from Canada, sails
-- regularly from a Canadian port and has an owner living or doing business in Canada, or is covered by a
-- Canada-and-flag-state agreement. In (b)(ii) the ship is read as the thing that is "regularly employed in voyages".
GIVEN `the employment is on a ship outside Canada or partly outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it would be insurable employment if it were in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the ship is of Canadian registry or licence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the ship is regularly employed in voyages between ports outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the ship has been chartered to a person resident outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the ship has been chartered to a person resident in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the ship is regularly employed in voyages from a port in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the operation of the ship is principally controlled in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the owner or managing owner of the ship resides or has a place of business in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any employment on the ship is subject to the provisions of the Act by virtue of an agreement between the Government of Canada and the government of the jurisdiction in which the ship is registered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 4 employment on a ship outside Canada` IF
        `the employment is on a ship outside Canada or partly outside Canada`
    AND `it would be insurable employment if it were in Canada`
    AND (   (   `the ship is of Canadian registry or licence`
            AND NOT (   `the ship is regularly employed in voyages between ports outside Canada`
                    AND `the ship has been chartered to a person resident outside Canada`))
         OR (   NOT (`the ship is of Canadian registry or licence`)
            AND (   (   `the ship has been chartered to a person resident in Canada`
                    AND `the ship is regularly employed in voyages from a port in Canada`)
                 OR (   `the operation of the ship is principally controlled in Canada`
                    AND `the ship is regularly employed in voyages from a port in Canada`
                    AND `the owner or managing owner of the ship resides or has a place of business in Canada`)
                 OR `any employment on the ship is subject to the provisions of the Act by virtue of an agreement between the Government of Canada and the government of the jurisdiction in which the ship is registered`)))

§ `Regulation 5 - employment outside Canada`

-- src:61 | 5 Employment outside Canada, other than employment on a ship described in section 4, is included in insurable employment if
-- src:62 | (a) the person so employed ordinarily resides in Canada;
-- src:63 | (b) that employment is outside Canada or partly outside Canada by an employer who is resident or has a place of business in Canada;
-- src:64 | (c) the employment would be insurable employment if it were in Canada; and
-- src:65 | (d) the employment is not insurable employment under the laws of the country in which it takes place.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 5 (src:61-65)
-- Plain gloss: work outside Canada, other than on a ship that reg 4 describes, counts as insurable if all four hold:
-- the worker usually lives in Canada, the employer lives or does business in Canada, the work would be insurable if
-- done in Canada, and the work is not insurable under the law of the country where it is done.
GIVEN `the employment is outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employment is on a ship described in section 4` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person so employed ordinarily resides in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employment is outside Canada or partly outside Canada by an employer who is resident or has a place of business in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employment would be insurable employment if it were in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employment is not insurable employment under the laws of the country in which it takes place` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 5 employment outside Canada` IF
        `the employment is outside Canada`
    AND NOT (`the employment is on a ship described in section 4`)
    AND `the person so employed ordinarily resides in Canada`
    AND `the employment is outside Canada or partly outside Canada by an employer who is resident or has a place of business in Canada`
    AND `the employment would be insurable employment if it were in Canada`
    AND `the employment is not insurable employment under the laws of the country in which it takes place`

§ `Regulation 6 - employments included in insurable employment`

-- Seven kinds of work are included. Each paragraph is a rule of its own; `reg 6 employment included` combines them
-- with the lead-in "unless it is excluded from insurable employment by any provision of these Regulations".
-- src:67 | (a) employment of a union member by the member's union in conducting union business, other than picketing in a labour dispute;
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 6(a) (src:67)
-- Plain gloss: a union member's work for their union on union business, but not picketing in a labour dispute.
GIVEN `the person is a union member employed by the member's union` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in conducting union business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the work is picketing in a labour dispute` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 6(a) employment of a union member by the member's union` IF
        `the person is a union member employed by the member's union`
    AND `in conducting union business`
    AND NOT (`the work is picketing in a labour dispute`)

-- src:68 | (b) employment of a person as an apprentice or trainee, notwithstanding that the person does not perform any services for their employer;
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 6(b) (src:68)
-- Plain gloss: an apprentice or trainee's work counts even if they do not perform any service for the employer.
GIVEN `the person is employed as an apprentice or trainee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 6(b) employment of a person as an apprentice or trainee` IF
    `the person is employed as an apprentice or trainee`

-- src:69 | (c) employment of a person as a member of the clergy or as a member of a religious order;
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 6(c) (src:69)
-- Plain gloss: work as a member of the clergy or of a religious order.
GIVEN `the person is employed as a member of the clergy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is employed as a member of a religious order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 6(c) employment of a person as a member of the clergy or of a religious order` IF
       `the person is employed as a member of the clergy`
    OR `the person is employed as a member of a religious order`

-- src:70 | (d) employment of a person in a barbering or hairdressing establishment, where the person
-- src:71 | (i) provides any of the services that are normally provided in such an establishment, and
-- src:72 | (ii) is not the owner or operator of the establishment;
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 6(d) (src:70-72)
-- Plain gloss: work in a barber's or hairdresser's shop, giving the services such a shop normally gives, unless the
-- person owns or runs the shop.
GIVEN `the person is employed in a barbering or hairdressing establishment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person provides any of the services that are normally provided in such an establishment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the owner or operator of the establishment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 6(d) employment in a barbering or hairdressing establishment` IF
        `the person is employed in a barbering or hairdressing establishment`
    AND `the person provides any of the services that are normally provided in such an establishment`
    AND NOT (`the person is the owner or operator of the establishment`)

-- src:73 | (e) employment of a person as a driver of a taxi, commercial bus, school bus or any other vehicle that is used by a business or public authority for carrying passengers, where the person is not the owner of more than 50 per cent of the vehicle or the owner or operator of the business or the operator of the public authority;
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 6(e) (src:73)
-- Plain gloss: work as the driver of a taxi, bus or other passenger vehicle used by a business or public authority,
-- unless the driver owns more than half the vehicle or owns or runs the business or authority. The portion owned is a
-- fraction (50 per cent is 0.5); more than 50 per cent takes the driver out, exactly 50 per cent does not.
GIVEN `the person is employed as a driver of a taxi, commercial bus, school bus or any other vehicle that is used by a business or public authority for carrying passengers` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the portion of the vehicle that the person owns` IS A NUMBER
      `the person is the owner or operator of the business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the operator of the public authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 6(e) employment as a driver of a vehicle that carries passengers` IF
        `the person is employed as a driver of a taxi, commercial bus, school bus or any other vehicle that is used by a business or public authority for carrying passengers`
    AND NOT (`the portion of the vehicle that the person owns` GREATER THAN 50%)
    AND NOT (`the person is the owner or operator of the business`)
    AND NOT (`the person is the operator of the public authority`)

-- src:74 | (f) employment of a person who holds an office, as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Canada Pension Plan,
-- src:75 | (i) in or under any department or other portion of the federal public administration set out in Schedule I, II, III, IV or V to the Financial Administration Act,
-- src:76 | (ii) where the person is appointed and remunerated under an Act governing the public service of a province, the government of which has, pursuant to subsection 2(1), agreed to insure all of its employees,
-- src:77 | (iii) where the person holds the office in or under a corporation, commission or other body that is an agent of Her Majesty in right of a province referred to in subparagraph (ii), or
-- src:78 | (iv) where the person holds the office in a union or an association of unions to which the person was elected by popular vote, or was elected or appointed to that office in the union or association in a representative capacity, and that employment is not included in insurable employment by paragraph (a); and
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 6(f) (src:74-78)
-- Plain gloss: work by someone who holds an "office" as the Canada Pension Plan defines it (a Canada Pension Plan
-- meaning, taken as one input), in (i) a federal department or other body in the Financial Administration Act schedules,
-- (ii) a province's public service where that province has agreed to insure all its employees under reg 2(1), (iii) a
-- body that is the agent of such a province, or (iv) a union or union association, elected by popular vote or elected
-- or appointed in a representative capacity, if that work is not already included by paragraph (a).
GIVEN `the person holds an office, as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Canada Pension Plan` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the office is in or under a department or other portion of the federal public administration set out in Schedule I, II, III, IV or V to the Financial Administration Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is appointed and remunerated under an Act governing the public service of a province, the government of which has, pursuant to subsection 2(1), agreed to insure all of its employees` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person holds the office in or under a corporation, commission or other body that is an agent of Her Majesty in right of a province referred to in subparagraph (ii)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person holds the office in a union or an association of unions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was elected to that office by popular vote` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was elected or appointed to that office in the union or association in a representative capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that employment is included in insurable employment by paragraph (a)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 6(f) employment of a person who holds an office` IF
        `the person holds an office, as defined in subsection 2(1) of the Canada Pension Plan`
    AND (   `the office is in or under a department or other portion of the federal public administration set out in Schedule I, II, III, IV or V to the Financial Administration Act`
         OR `the person is appointed and remunerated under an Act governing the public service of a province, the government of which has, pursuant to subsection 2(1), agreed to insure all of its employees`
         OR `the person holds the office in or under a corporation, commission or other body that is an agent of Her Majesty in right of a province referred to in subparagraph (ii)`
         OR (   `the person holds the office in a union or an association of unions`
            AND (   `the person was elected to that office by popular vote`
                 OR `the person was elected or appointed to that office in the union or association in a representative capacity`)
            AND NOT (`that employment is included in insurable employment by paragraph (a)`)))

-- src:79 | (g) employment of a person who is placed in that employment by a placement or employment agency to perform services for and under the direction and control of a client of the agency, where that person is remunerated by the agency for the performance of those services.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 6(g) (src:79)
-- Plain gloss: work for a client of a placement or employment agency, under the client's direction and control, where
-- the agency placed the person and pays them for it.
GIVEN `the person is placed in that employment by a placement or employment agency` IS A BOOLEAN
      `to perform services for and under the direction and control of a client of the agency` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is remunerated by the agency for the performance of those services` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 6(g) employment of a person who is placed by a placement or employment agency` IF
        `the person is placed in that employment by a placement or employment agency`
    AND `to perform services for and under the direction and control of a client of the agency`
    AND `the person is remunerated by the agency for the performance of those services`

-- src:66 | 6 Employment in any of the following employments, unless it is excluded from insurable employment by any provision of these Regulations, is included in insurable employment:
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 6 (src:66)
-- Plain gloss: the work is included if it falls in any of paragraphs (a) to (g) and no provision of the Regulations
-- (regs 7 to 9, and any other provision of these Regulations: one input) excludes it.
GIVEN `paragraph (a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (d)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (e)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (f)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (g)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is excluded from insurable employment by any provision of these Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 6 employment included` IF
        (   `paragraph (a)`
         OR `paragraph (b)`
         OR `paragraph (c)`
         OR `paragraph (d)`
         OR `paragraph (e)`
         OR `paragraph (f)`
         OR `paragraph (g)`)
    AND NOT (`it is excluded from insurable employment by any provision of these Regulations`)

-- src:51 | 2 (1) Employment in Canada by Her Majesty in right of a province that would, except for paragraph 5(2)(c) of the Act, be insurable employment is included in insurable employment if the government of the province enters into an agreement with the Commission whereby that government agrees to waive exclusion and to insure all its employees engaged in such employment.
-- src:53 | 3 (1) Employment in Canada by the government of a country other than Canada or of any political subdivision of that other country, or by an international organization, that would, except for paragraphs 5(2)(d) and (e) of the Act, be insurable employment, may be included in insurable employment if the employing government or the international organization, as the case may be, consents in writing to its inclusion.
-- src:55 | 4 Employment on a ship outside Canada or partly outside Canada that would be insurable employment if it were in Canada is included in insurable employment if that employment is
-- src:61 | 5 Employment outside Canada, other than employment on a ship described in section 4, is included in insurable employment if
-- src:66 | 6 Employment in any of the following employments, unless it is excluded from insurable employment by any provision of these Regulations, is included in insurable employment:
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations regs 2 to 6 (src:51) (src:53) (src:55) (src:61) (src:66)
-- Plain gloss: the Regulations include the work in insurable employment if reg 2(1), reg 3(1), reg 4, reg 5 or reg 6
-- says so. This is the one BOOLEAN that the core's `s 5(1)(d) employment included by regulations` takes. (Regs 2(1)
-- and 3(1) also feed the core's `s 5(2)(c)`, `(d)` and `(e)` directly; keel fork F2 in KEEL-NOTES.md.)
GIVEN `reg 2(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reg 3(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reg 4` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reg 5` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reg 6` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 2 to 6 employment included in insurable employment` IF
       `reg 2(1)`
    OR `reg 3(1)`
    OR `reg 4`
    OR `reg 5`
    OR `reg 6`

§ `Regulation 7 - employments excluded from insurable employment`

-- Paragraph (a) of reg 7 is repealed in this text; the stub below is documentation, not a rule.
-- src:83 | (a) [Repealed, SOR/97-310, s. 1]
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 7(a) (src:83)
`reg 7(a) repealed in this text` MEANS "reg 7(a): [Repealed, SOR/97-310, s. 1]"

-- src:84 | (b) employment of a person who is a member of a religious order, if the person has taken a vow of poverty and the person's remuneration is paid directly, or by that person, to the order;
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 7(b) (src:84)
-- Plain gloss: a member of a religious order who has taken a vow of poverty, whose pay goes to the order (directly,
-- or through the member).
GIVEN `the person is a member of a religious order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has taken a vow of poverty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person's remuneration is paid directly to the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person's remuneration is paid by that person to the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 7(b) employment of a member of a religious order who has taken a vow of poverty` IF
        `the person is a member of a religious order`
    AND `the person has taken a vow of poverty`
    AND (   `the person's remuneration is paid directly to the order`
         OR `the person's remuneration is paid by that person to the order`)

-- src:85 | (c) employment in respect of which premiums are payable under
-- src:86 | (i) the unemployment insurance law of any state of the United States, the District of Columbia, Puerto Rico or the Virgin Islands, by reason of the Agreement between Canada and the United States Respecting Unemployment Insurance, signed on March 6 and 12, 1942, or
-- src:87 | (ii) the Railroad Unemployment Insurance Act of the United States;
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 7(c) (src:85-87)
-- Plain gloss: work for which premiums are payable under a United States state's unemployment insurance law (by reason
-- of the 1942 Canada-United States Agreement) or under the United States Railroad Unemployment Insurance Act.
GIVEN `premiums are payable under the unemployment insurance law of any state of the United States, the District of Columbia, Puerto Rico or the Virgin Islands` IS A BOOLEAN
      `by reason of the Agreement between Canada and the United States Respecting Unemployment Insurance, signed on March 6 and 12, 1942` IS A BOOLEAN
      `premiums are payable under the Railroad Unemployment Insurance Act of the United States` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 7(c) employment in respect of which premiums are payable under the law of the United States` IF
        (   `premiums are payable under the unemployment insurance law of any state of the United States, the District of Columbia, Puerto Rico or the Virgin Islands`
        AND `by reason of the Agreement between Canada and the United States Respecting Unemployment Insurance, signed on March 6 and 12, 1942`)
    OR  `premiums are payable under the Railroad Unemployment Insurance Act of the United States`

-- src:88 | (d) employment in Canada of a person who resides in a country other than Canada, if premiums are payable in respect of services performed by the person in Canada under the unemployment insurance laws of that other country;
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 7(d) (src:88)
-- Plain gloss: work done in Canada by someone who lives in another country, if premiums are payable for those
-- services under that other country's unemployment insurance laws.
GIVEN `the employment is in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person resides in a country other than Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `premiums are payable in respect of services performed by the person in Canada under the unemployment insurance laws of that other country` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 7(d) employment in Canada of a person who resides in another country` IF
        `the employment is in Canada`
    AND `the person resides in a country other than Canada`
    AND `premiums are payable in respect of services performed by the person in Canada under the unemployment insurance laws of that other country`

-- src:89 | (e) employment of a person for the purpose of a rescue operation, if the person is not regularly employed by the employer who employs them for that purpose; and
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 7(e) (src:89)
-- Plain gloss: work on a rescue operation by someone the employer does not regularly employ.
GIVEN `the employment is for the purpose of a rescue operation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is regularly employed by the employer who employs them for that purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 7(e) employment for the purpose of a rescue operation` IF
        `the employment is for the purpose of a rescue operation`
    AND NOT (`the person is regularly employed by the employer who employs them for that purpose`)

-- src:90 | (f) employment under an employment support measure referred to in paragraph 59(b) of the Act — or a measure that is the subject of an agreement under section 63 of the Act — that is established to
-- src:91 | (i) help insured participants start businesses or become self-employed, or
-- src:92 | (ii) provide insured participants with employment opportunities through which they can gain work experience to improve their long-term employment prospects.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 7(f) (src:90-92)
-- Plain gloss: work under an employment support measure (the Act's paragraph 59(b), or a measure under an agreement
-- under its section 63, both outside this piece: piece ei2) set up to help insured participants start a business or
-- become self-employed, or to give them work experience that improves their long-term job prospects.
GIVEN `the employment is under an employment support measure referred to in paragraph 59(b) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employment is under a measure that is the subject of an agreement under section 63 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the measure is established to help insured participants start businesses or become self-employed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the measure is established to provide insured participants with employment opportunities through which they can gain work experience to improve their long-term employment prospects` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 7(f) employment under an employment support measure` IF
        (   `the employment is under an employment support measure referred to in paragraph 59(b) of the Act`
         OR `the employment is under a measure that is the subject of an agreement under section 63 of the Act`)
    AND (   `the measure is established to help insured participants start businesses or become self-employed`
         OR `the measure is established to provide insured participants with employment opportunities through which they can gain work experience to improve their long-term employment prospects`)

-- src:82 | 7 The following employments are excluded from insurable employment:
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 7 (src:82)
-- Plain gloss: any one of paragraphs (b) to (f) excludes the work. (Paragraph (a) is repealed.)
GIVEN `paragraph (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (d)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (e)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (f)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 7 employment excluded` IF
       `paragraph (b)`
    OR `paragraph (c)`
    OR `paragraph (d)`
    OR `paragraph (e)`
    OR `paragraph (f)`

§ `Regulation 8 - short employments excluded, and when they become insurable`

-- A point in time at which an employment becomes insurable: reg 8(2) and (4) say "the day or ... the hour, as the case
-- may be". The stable binary's datetime library is not used; a day and an hour of the day (0 to 23) are enough.
-- src:101 | (2) Where an employment that has been excluded from insurable employment under paragraph (1)(a) or (c) becomes a regular employment, the employment is insurable employment beginning on the day or at the hour, as the case may be, that the employment became a regular employment.
-- src:103 | (4) Where a person has been employed by the same employer in one or more employments that have been excluded from insurable employment under paragraph (1)(c) and the total period of those employments exceeds 34 hours in the same year, the employments, taken together, are insurable employment beginning at the hour when the total period of employment began.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 8(2) and (4) (src:101) (src:103)
DECLARE `er1 Day and hour` HAS
    `er1 the day`                          IS A DATE
    `er1 the hour of the day, 0 to 23`     IS A NUMBER

-- src:94 | (a) employment of a person by an employer, other than as an entertainer, in connection with a circus, fair, parade, carnival, exposition, exhibition or other similar activity if the person
-- src:95 | (i) is not regularly employed by that employer, and
-- src:96 | (ii) is employed by that employer in that employment for less than seven days in a year; and
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 8(1)(a) (src:94-96)
-- Plain gloss: a short job at a circus, fair, parade, carnival, exposition, exhibition or similar activity, other than
-- as an entertainer, for an employer who does not regularly employ the person and for fewer than seven days in the year.
-- Subject to reg 8(2) and (3) below, which can make the same job insurable.
GIVEN `the employment is in connection with a circus, fair, parade, carnival, exposition, exhibition or other similar activity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is employed as an entertainer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is regularly employed by that employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of days in the year for which the person is employed by that employer in that employment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 8(1)(a) employment in connection with a circus, fair or similar activity` IF
        `the employment is in connection with a circus, fair, parade, carnival, exposition, exhibition or other similar activity`
    AND NOT (`the person is employed as an entertainer`)
    AND NOT (`the person is regularly employed by that employer`)
    AND `the number of days in the year for which the person is employed by that employer in that employment` LESS THAN 7

-- src:97 | (b) [Repealed, SOR/98-588, s. 1]
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 8(1)(b) (src:97)
`reg 8(1)(b) repealed in this text` MEANS "reg 8(1)(b): [Repealed, SOR/98-588, s. 1]"

-- src:98 | (c) employment of a person by Her Majesty in right of Canada, the government of a province, a municipality or a school board in connection with a referendum or election to public office if the person
-- src:99 | (i) is not regularly employed by that employer, and
-- src:100 | (ii) is employed by that employer in that employment for less than 35 hours in any year after 1998.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 8(1)(c) (src:98-100)
-- Plain gloss: a short job for the federal government, a provincial government, a municipality or a school board in
-- connection with a referendum or an election to public office, for an employer who does not regularly employ the
-- person and for fewer than 35 hours in a year after 1998. The text only speaks of "any year after 1998": for 1998
-- and earlier years this paragraph does not apply (the test of subparagraph (ii) cannot be met).
-- Subject to reg 8(2) and (4) below.
GIVEN `the employer is Her Majesty in right of Canada, the government of a province, a municipality or a school board` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employment is in connection with a referendum or election to public office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is regularly employed by that employer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of hours in the year for which the person is employed by that employer in that employment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 8(1)(c) employment in connection with a referendum or election` IF
        `the employer is Her Majesty in right of Canada, the government of a province, a municipality or a school board`
    AND `the employment is in connection with a referendum or election to public office`
    AND NOT (`the person is regularly employed by that employer`)
    AND `the year` GREATER THAN 1998
    AND `the number of hours in the year for which the person is employed by that employer in that employment` LESS THAN 35

-- src:101 | (2) Where an employment that has been excluded from insurable employment under paragraph (1)(a) or (c) becomes a regular employment, the employment is insurable employment beginning on the day or at the hour, as the case may be, that the employment became a regular employment.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 8(2) (src:101)
-- Plain gloss: if a job that was excluded under (1)(a) or (c) turns into regular employment, it is insurable from the day
-- (or the hour, for an (1)(c) job) it became regular. NOTHING when it was not excluded or has not become regular.
GIVEN `the employment has been excluded from insurable employment under paragraph (1)(a) or (c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employment becomes a regular employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day and hour at which it became a regular employment` IS A `er1 Day and hour`
GIVETH A MAYBE `er1 Day and hour`
DECIDE `reg 8(2) the point from which the employment is insurable` IS
    IF `the employment has been excluded from insurable employment under paragraph (1)(a) or (c)` AND `the employment becomes a regular employment`
    THEN JUST `the day and hour at which it became a regular employment`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:102 | (3) Where a person has been employed by the same employer in one or more employments that have been excluded from insurable employment under paragraph (1)(a) and the total period of those employments exceeds six days in the same year, the employments, taken together, are insurable employment beginning on the day when the total period of employment began.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 8(3) (src:102)
-- Plain gloss: if several (1)(a) jobs with the same employer add up to more than six days in the year, together they are
-- insurable from the day the first of them began. NOTHING when the total is six days or fewer.
GIVEN `the person has been employed by the same employer in one or more employments excluded from insurable employment under paragraph (1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the total period of those employments in the same year, in days` IS A NUMBER
      `the day when the total period of employment began` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `reg 8(3) the day from which the employments taken together are insurable` IS
    IF `the person has been employed by the same employer in one or more employments excluded from insurable employment under paragraph (1)(a)` AND `the total period of those employments in the same year, in days` GREATER THAN 6
    THEN JUST `the day when the total period of employment began`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:103 | (4) Where a person has been employed by the same employer in one or more employments that have been excluded from insurable employment under paragraph (1)(c) and the total period of those employments exceeds 34 hours in the same year, the employments, taken together, are insurable employment beginning at the hour when the total period of employment began.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 8(4) (src:103)
-- Plain gloss: if several (1)(c) jobs with the same employer add up to more than 34 hours in the year, together they are
-- insurable from the hour the first of them began. NOTHING when the total is 34 hours or fewer.
GIVEN `the person has been employed by the same employer in one or more employments excluded from insurable employment under paragraph (1)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the total period of those employments in the same year, in hours` IS A NUMBER
      `the day and hour when the total period of employment began` IS A `er1 Day and hour`
GIVETH A MAYBE `er1 Day and hour`
DECIDE `reg 8(4) the hour from which the employments taken together are insurable` IS
    IF `the person has been employed by the same employer in one or more employments excluded from insurable employment under paragraph (1)(c)` AND `the total period of those employments in the same year, in hours` GREATER THAN 34
    THEN JUST `the day and hour when the total period of employment began`
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Regulation 9 - farm work`

-- src:105 | agriculture means the operations of farming that are carried out for the benefit of any person who is a farmer and, without limiting the generality of the foregoing, includes
-- src:106 | (a) where carried out on a farm
-- src:107 | (i) clearing land for cultivation,
-- src:108 | (ii) cultivation of the soil,
-- src:109 | (iii) conservation of the soil, including the construction, maintenance and operation of tile drainage systems, ditches, canals, reservoirs or waterways exclusively for the purposes of farming,
-- src:110 | (iv) harvesting, storing or grading any natural product of farming,
-- src:111 | (v) preparing land for the growing and harvesting of wild berries,
-- src:112 | (vi) raising bees and producing honey,
-- src:113 | (vii) breeding or raising animals or birds, or producing eggs,
-- src:114 | (viii) dairy farming and the processing of milk, butter or cheese that is produced on that farm, and
-- src:115 | (ix) producing maple sap, maple syrup or maple sugar; and
-- src:116 | (b) where carried out on or off a farm
-- src:117 | (i) offering for sale or selling any of the products of the operations referred to in subparagraphs (a) (i) to (ix), if the offering for sale or selling is incidental to those operations, and
-- src:118 | (ii) exhibiting, advertising, assembling, freezing, storing, grading, preparing, processing, packing and transporting the products described in subparagraph (i), if those operations are incidental to the offering for sale or selling described in that subparagraph. (agriculture)
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 9(1) "agriculture" (src:105-118)
-- The definition lists operations that "agriculture" includes, "without limiting the generality" of the opening words.
-- So the listed operations are agriculture in themselves, and any other operation is agriculture if it is
-- "the operations of farming ... carried out for the benefit of any person who is a farmer" (fork F4 in NOTES.md).
DECLARE `er1 Operation that the definition of agriculture lists` IS ONE OF
    `er1 (a)(i) clearing land for cultivation`
    `er1 (a)(ii) cultivation of the soil`
    `er1 (a)(iii) conservation of the soil, including the construction, maintenance and operation of tile drainage systems, ditches, canals, reservoirs or waterways exclusively for the purposes of farming`
    `er1 (a)(iv) harvesting, storing or grading any natural product of farming`
    `er1 (a)(v) preparing land for the growing and harvesting of wild berries`
    `er1 (a)(vi) raising bees and producing honey`
    `er1 (a)(vii) breeding or raising animals or birds, or producing eggs`
    `er1 (a)(viii) dairy farming and the processing of milk, butter or cheese that is produced on that farm`
    `er1 (a)(ix) producing maple sap, maple syrup or maple sugar`
    `er1 (b)(i) offering for sale or selling any of the products of the operations referred to in subparagraphs (a)(i) to (ix)`
    `er1 (b)(ii) exhibiting, advertising, assembling, freezing, storing, grading, preparing, processing, packing and transporting the products described in subparagraph (i)`
    `er1 an operation that the definition does not list`

-- src:105 | agriculture means the operations of farming that are carried out for the benefit of any person who is a farmer and, without limiting the generality of the foregoing, includes
-- src:106 | (a) where carried out on a farm
-- src:107 | (i) clearing land for cultivation,
-- src:108 | (ii) cultivation of the soil,
-- src:109 | (iii) conservation of the soil, including the construction, maintenance and operation of tile drainage systems, ditches, canals, reservoirs or waterways exclusively for the purposes of farming,
-- src:110 | (iv) harvesting, storing or grading any natural product of farming,
-- src:111 | (v) preparing land for the growing and harvesting of wild berries,
-- src:112 | (vi) raising bees and producing honey,
-- src:113 | (vii) breeding or raising animals or birds, or producing eggs,
-- src:114 | (viii) dairy farming and the processing of milk, butter or cheese that is produced on that farm, and
-- src:115 | (ix) producing maple sap, maple syrup or maple sugar; and
-- src:116 | (b) where carried out on or off a farm
-- src:117 | (i) offering for sale or selling any of the products of the operations referred to in subparagraphs (a) (i) to (ix), if the offering for sale or selling is incidental to those operations, and
-- src:118 | (ii) exhibiting, advertising, assembling, freezing, storing, grading, preparing, processing, packing and transporting the products described in subparagraph (i), if those operations are incidental to the offering for sale or selling described in that subparagraph. (agriculture)
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 9(1) "agriculture" (src:105-118)
-- Plain gloss: the listed farm operations done on a farm (paragraph (a)) and the selling and handling of farm products
-- that is incidental to them, on or off a farm (paragraph (b)).
GIVEN operation IS A `er1 Operation that the definition of agriculture lists`
      `it is carried out on a farm` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offering for sale or selling is incidental to those operations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `those operations are incidental to the offering for sale or selling described in subparagraph (i)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 9(1) agriculture, listed operations` IS
    CONSIDER operation
    WHEN `er1 (b)(i) offering for sale or selling any of the products of the operations referred to in subparagraphs (a)(i) to (ix)` THEN `the offering for sale or selling is incidental to those operations`
    WHEN `er1 (b)(ii) exhibiting, advertising, assembling, freezing, storing, grading, preparing, processing, packing and transporting the products described in subparagraph (i)` THEN `those operations are incidental to the offering for sale or selling described in subparagraph (i)`
    WHEN `er1 an operation that the definition does not list` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE `it is carried out on a farm`

-- src:105 | agriculture means the operations of farming that are carried out for the benefit of any person who is a farmer and, without limiting the generality of the foregoing, includes
-- src:106 | (a) where carried out on a farm
-- src:107 | (i) clearing land for cultivation,
-- src:108 | (ii) cultivation of the soil,
-- src:109 | (iii) conservation of the soil, including the construction, maintenance and operation of tile drainage systems, ditches, canals, reservoirs or waterways exclusively for the purposes of farming,
-- src:110 | (iv) harvesting, storing or grading any natural product of farming,
-- src:111 | (v) preparing land for the growing and harvesting of wild berries,
-- src:112 | (vi) raising bees and producing honey,
-- src:113 | (vii) breeding or raising animals or birds, or producing eggs,
-- src:114 | (viii) dairy farming and the processing of milk, butter or cheese that is produced on that farm, and
-- src:115 | (ix) producing maple sap, maple syrup or maple sugar; and
-- src:116 | (b) where carried out on or off a farm
-- src:117 | (i) offering for sale or selling any of the products of the operations referred to in subparagraphs (a) (i) to (ix), if the offering for sale or selling is incidental to those operations, and
-- src:118 | (ii) exhibiting, advertising, assembling, freezing, storing, grading, preparing, processing, packing and transporting the products described in subparagraph (i), if those operations are incidental to the offering for sale or selling described in that subparagraph. (agriculture)
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 9(1) "agriculture" (src:105)
GIVEN operation IS A `er1 Operation that the definition of agriculture lists`
      `it is carried out on a farm` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offering for sale or selling is incidental to those operations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `those operations are incidental to the offering for sale or selling described in subparagraph (i)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is operations of farming carried out for the benefit of a person who is a farmer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 9(1) agriculture` IF
        `it is operations of farming carried out for the benefit of a person who is a farmer`
    OR  `reg 9(1) agriculture, listed operations` operation `it is carried out on a farm` `the offering for sale or selling is incidental to those operations` `those operations are incidental to the offering for sale or selling described in subparagraph (i)`

-- src:119 | agricultural enterprise means the business of agriculture carried on for the benefit of any person who is a farmer. (entreprise agricole)
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 9(1) "agricultural enterprise" (src:119)
-- Plain gloss: a farming business run for a farmer.
GIVEN `it is the business of agriculture` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is carried on for the benefit of a person who is a farmer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 9(1) agricultural enterprise` IF
        `it is the business of agriculture`
    AND `it is carried on for the benefit of a person who is a farmer`

-- src:120 | horticulture means the following operations and includes all the services incidental to the carrying out of those operations, if the services are performed at the place where the operations are carried on:
-- src:121 | (a) the propagating, producing, raising or harvesting of
-- src:122 | (i) vegetables, flowers, shrubs or ornamental grasses, and
-- src:123 | (ii) seeds, seedlings, grafts or cuttings of vegetables, flowers, shrubs or ornamental grasses; and
-- src:124 | (b) landscape gardening where it is incidental to the carrying out of
-- src:125 | (i) any of the operations described in paragraph (a), or
-- src:126 | (ii) agriculture. (horticulture)
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 9(1) "horticulture" (src:120-126)
-- "(a) ... (i) vegetables, ... and (ii) seeds, seedlings, grafts or cuttings ..." lists two products of one operation, so
-- either is horticulture (the "and" joins kinds that each stand alone; fork F5 in NOTES.md).
DECLARE `er1 Operation that the definition of horticulture describes` IS ONE OF
    `er1 (a)(i) propagating, producing, raising or harvesting vegetables, flowers, shrubs or ornamental grasses`
    `er1 (a)(ii) propagating, producing, raising or harvesting seeds, seedlings, grafts or cuttings of vegetables, flowers, shrubs or ornamental grasses`
    `er1 (b) landscape gardening`
    `er1 a service incidental to carrying out those operations`
    `er1 an operation that the definition does not describe`

-- src:120 | horticulture means the following operations and includes all the services incidental to the carrying out of those operations, if the services are performed at the place where the operations are carried on:
-- src:121 | (a) the propagating, producing, raising or harvesting of
-- src:122 | (i) vegetables, flowers, shrubs or ornamental grasses, and
-- src:123 | (ii) seeds, seedlings, grafts or cuttings of vegetables, flowers, shrubs or ornamental grasses; and
-- src:124 | (b) landscape gardening where it is incidental to the carrying out of
-- src:125 | (i) any of the operations described in paragraph (a), or
-- src:126 | (ii) agriculture. (horticulture)
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 9(1) "horticulture" (src:120-126)
-- Plain gloss: growing vegetables, flowers, shrubs or ornamental grasses or their seeds, seedlings, grafts or cuttings;
-- landscape gardening that goes with that growing or with agriculture; and services that go with those operations,
-- when done where the operations are carried on.
GIVEN operation IS A `er1 Operation that the definition of horticulture describes`
      `the landscape gardening is incidental to the carrying out of any of the operations described in paragraph (a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the landscape gardening is incidental to the carrying out of agriculture` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the services are performed at the place where the operations are carried on` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 9(1) horticulture` IS
    CONSIDER operation
    WHEN `er1 (a)(i) propagating, producing, raising or harvesting vegetables, flowers, shrubs or ornamental grasses` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `er1 (a)(ii) propagating, producing, raising or harvesting seeds, seedlings, grafts or cuttings of vegetables, flowers, shrubs or ornamental grasses` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `er1 (b) landscape gardening` THEN (   `the landscape gardening is incidental to the carrying out of any of the operations described in paragraph (a)`
                                           OR `the landscape gardening is incidental to the carrying out of agriculture`)
    WHEN `er1 a service incidental to carrying out those operations` THEN `the services are performed at the place where the operations are carried on`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- src:127 | (2) The employment of a person by an employer in agriculture, an agricultural enterprise or horticulture that would otherwise be insurable is excluded from insurable employment if the person is employed by the employer in that employment for
-- src:128 | (a) less than seven days in a year; or
-- src:129 | (b) seven days or more in a year and is not remunerated in cash by the employer for any part of that employment.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 9(2) (src:127-129)
-- Plain gloss: farm, farm-business or horticulture work that would otherwise be insurable is excluded if the person works
-- for the employer for fewer than seven days in the year, or for seven days or more but is not paid any cash.
GIVEN `the employment would otherwise be insurable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is employed by the employer in agriculture` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is employed by the employer in an agricultural enterprise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is employed by the employer in horticulture` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of days in a year for which the person is employed by the employer in that employment` IS A NUMBER
      `the person is remunerated in cash by the employer for any part of that employment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 9(2) employment in agriculture, an agricultural enterprise or horticulture` IF
        `the employment would otherwise be insurable`
    AND (   `the person is employed by the employer in agriculture`
         OR `the person is employed by the employer in an agricultural enterprise`
         OR `the person is employed by the employer in horticulture`)
    AND (   `the number of days in a year for which the person is employed by the employer in that employment` LESS THAN 7
         OR (   `the number of days in a year for which the person is employed by the employer in that employment` AT LEAST 7
            AND NOT (`the person is remunerated in cash by the employer for any part of that employment`)))

-- src:82 | 7 The following employments are excluded from insurable employment:
-- src:93 | 8 (1) Subject to subsections (2) to (4), the following employments are excluded from insurable employment:
-- src:127 | (2) The employment of a person by an employer in agriculture, an agricultural enterprise or horticulture that would otherwise be insurable is excluded from insurable employment if the person is employed by the employer in that employment for
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations regs 7 to 9 (src:82) (src:93) (src:127)
-- Plain gloss: the Regulations exclude the work if reg 7 or reg 9(2) says so, or if reg 8(1)(a) or (c) says so and
-- reg 8(2), (3) or (4) has not by then made it insurable. This is the one BOOLEAN that the core's
-- `s 5(2)(h) employment excluded by regulations` takes. The time at which reg 8(2) to (4) is tested is the time the
-- question is asked about; those rules give the point from which the work is insurable.
GIVEN `reg 7` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reg 8(1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reg 8(1)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reg 8(2), (3) or (4) has made the employment insurable at the time in question` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reg 9(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 7 to 9 employment excluded from insurable employment` IF
        `reg 7`
    OR  (   (   `reg 8(1)(a)`
            OR `reg 8(1)(c)`)
        AND NOT (`reg 8(2), (3) or (4) has made the employment insurable at the time in question`))
    OR  `reg 9(2)`
